WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.169
Moments ago, Chinese President Xi Jinping,
as you can see here,

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:06.973
landing in Moscow for his face
to face meeting with President Putin.

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:10.510
On the agenda, obviously, Ukraine,
she said that he believes

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.747
China is actively promoting peace talks
while Putin

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.017
was in the Russian occupied Ukrainian city
of Mariupol over the weekend.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:20.353
Says he welcomes China's, quote, readiness
to make

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:23.223
a meaningful contribution
to the settlement of the crisis.

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:25.725
The White House is John Kirby
joins us now.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:26.860
Good morning, John.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:30.697
Are you expecting any tangible agreements
to come out of this summit

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.732
with Putin and Xi?

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.234
Difficult to know, Caitlin.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.002
Obviously,
we're not part of these discussions,

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:40.206
so we'll see what these two leaders
actually come out and say

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:40.907
at the end of this.

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:44.511
I guess it's going to be a couple of days
here of of their meeting and that agenda.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:45.645
So we'll see.

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:48.681
But as you know,
we've we've been very, very public

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:52.385
about any concerns about some sort
of a cease fire announcement.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:55.121
Right now, we all want to see peace.
We all want to see this war end.

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:57.290
It could end today
if Mr. Putin did the right thing.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.625
But a cease fire called

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:02.262
right now would basically just ratify
Russia's conquest and give Mr.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:07.400
Putin more time to reequip and retrain
and and restart operations at a time

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.868
and a place of his choosing.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:13.373
So if they call for a cease fire, you believe Ukraine should and will reject that?

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.375
Yes, we do.

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:17.277
And we would reject it as well.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:19.879
We think that
that's an unacceptable outcome right now.

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:22.115
Obviously, we want the fighting to stop.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.349
We want the war to be over.

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:26.086
And as I said, it could end today
if Mr. Putin would do the right thing.

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:29.355
But to call for a cease fire right
now, basically ratifies

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:33.493
what they've been able to grab inside
Ukraine and gives them time and space

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.562
to prepare for future operations.

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:37.230
And that's
just not going to be acceptable.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:41.034
John, do you think this meeting could be
a venue where they announce that China

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:45.305
may start providing weapons to Ukraine
or to Russia to use in Ukraine?

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:48.942
We don't believe it's in China's
best interest to do that.

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:50.443
We can't

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.880
we can't envision how they would think
that it's in their best interests

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:54.447
to help Mr.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:57.183
Putin continue to slaughter
more innocent Ukrainians.

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.818
So we don't want to see that again.

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:00.353
We'll see what these leaders come out with

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.989
and what they say
at the end of these discussions.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:05.125
We're going to watch this very,
very closely.

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:06.659
Again, we have communicated

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:09.729
privately to the Chinese
we've certainly communicated it publicly

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:13.533
that that would not be an outcome
that's to the betterment not only of China

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.200
and their interests,

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.270
but certainly to the Ukrainian people
and to the whole idea of peace.

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:20.640
What does it say to you that after
the International Criminal Court

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.711
issued that arrest warrant for Putin,
that she still showed up in Russia?

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.412
It clearly did not deter that visit.

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:30.183
But also, you saw Putin over the weekend
in Mariupol in all of these other cities.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:33.119
I think you have to
it's your first question.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:36.222
I think he got to keep this relationship
in some sort of context here.

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:40.326
These are two nations
who chafe and bristle at the idea of U.S.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.362
leadership
or U.S. influence around the world.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:45.165
They don't
they don't like playing by the rules

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:48.134
that the world order has in place.

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:49.869
And they want to challenge
U.S. leadership.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:52.138
This is a marriage of convenience,
not of affection.

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:54.541
These are two countries that don't have

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:56.743
a heck of a whole lot of trust
between one another.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:03:00.647
But they find common cause in pushing
back on the West and pushing back on

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:01.981
American leadership.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:05.084
So, again, we'll see what they decide
to do when they come out with this.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:07.787
And as for Mr. Putin's visit to Mariupol.

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:12.926
Mariupol is far away from the front lines
of the fighting in the south

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:14.093
and in the east.

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:18.131
It was a convenient excuse for him
to go in advance of Xi's visit

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:21.834
to show that he's still the commander
in chief, that he's still in charge,

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:26.639
and that his military still has occupied
territory inside Ukraine.

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:30.310
There's no doubt that
that he could see for himself,

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.011
or we would hope
that he would see for himself

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:35.648
how badly his military is actually doing,
where the fighting is actually occurring.

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:39.452
And not most of that is right up now
in the Donbass near a town called Back.

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.589
The White House wanted President
Xi to also speak

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:45.425
with President Dolinsky
to get the Ukrainian perspective in this.

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:48.027
Any indication that's going to happen?

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.596
We haven't seen any confirmation of it.

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:52.398
Obviously, President Xi would be the one
to announce that if he's going to do it.

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:55.168
But we absolutely have been suggesting it
for quite some time.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:56.636
And we'd love to see that happen.

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:58.171
I mean, if you're going to go to Moscow

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:00.340
and you're going to sit down
for three days with President Putin

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:03.042
and you're going to get his perspective
on a war that he started

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:06.179
and that he could finish today,
you ought to pick up the phone at the very

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:09.782
least and talk to President Zelensky
and get the Ukrainian perspective here.

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:12.085
What we've been saying
from the very beginning,

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:13.152
if this comes down to some

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:16.689
kind of negotiated settlement of some sort
and some place at some time,

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:19.292
it's got to be nothing about Ukraine
without Ukraine.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:22.629
So Ukraine has got to be central
to those discussions.

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:25.431
Their perspectives
have to be heard and respected

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:28.101
so we absolutely want President
Xi to reach out

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:32.038
and get a little bit of the views
and perspective of Ukraine here.

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:34.140
It's been about a week since President
Biden said

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:36.376
he was going to speak to President
Xi soon.

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:38.578
Is that call and scheduled yet, John?

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:41.047
It hasn't been scheduled, Caitlin,

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:44.717
but the president very much wants to have
another conversation with President Xi.

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:46.386
It's really important
that we keep these lines

00:04:46.386 --> 00:04:47.620
of communication open

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:50.490
between the United States and China,
the most consequential bilateral

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:51.758
relationship in the world.

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:54.160
President wants to keep those lines
open. Will do that.

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:56.996
And he'll have a call with President
Xi at the appropriate time.

00:04:57.764 --> 00:04:59.165
What is the appropriate time?

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:01.501
Because he said back in mid-February
after the U.S.

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:04.437
down to that surveillance balloon,
that he would speak to him soon.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.072
He said last we could speak to him soon.

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:10.176
So as the US tried to schedule the call
on, the Chinese have been unwilling

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:11.311
or what's going on here?

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:13.046
No, there's been no logistics.

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:15.214
There's been
no there's been no setting it up.

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:20.186
We we maintain that we're going to have
another discussion with President Xi.

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:23.022
The president wants to do
that, wants to keep those lines open

00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:25.258
and at the appropriate time,
we'll reach out

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:27.060
and we'll see
if we can get a call on the schedule.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.995
These are two men
that also know each other

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:30.963
for quite some time
when they were both vice

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:32.598
presidents of their respective countries.

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:35.034
They had a good meeting in Bali,
a good discussion.

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:37.370
We'd like to continue that discussion.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:41.040
We'd like to make sure that this
bilateral relationship is serving

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:45.178
not only the best interests
of the American people but also the world.

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:49.782
And this is a relationship that needs to
be handled in a responsible, mature way.

00:05:49.816 --> 00:05:52.852
We want to get back to that,
but we're just going to have to wait

00:05:53.086 --> 00:05:54.654
and and do that at the right time.

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:55.421
Speaking of open

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:59.826
lines of communication, we're seeing North
Korea continue to fire off projectiles.

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:01.361
Is it still accurate to say there's

00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:04.263
been no contact between the Biden
administration and North Korea?

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:07.367
Not for lack of
try and enough for lack of interest.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:11.637
Caitlin, we maintain that we would still,
without precondition,

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:14.907
be willing to sit down
and with the North Korean regime

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:19.879
and try to find a diplomatic way
to reduce the nuclear tensions

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:23.049
on the peninsula
and to see the verifiable denuclearization

00:06:24.117 --> 00:06:25.551
of of North Korea.

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:28.688
But they have yet to show any interest
in that whatsoever,

00:06:28.688 --> 00:06:30.423
any communication whatsoever.

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:31.257
Quite the contrary.

00:06:31.257 --> 00:06:34.327
As you rightly noted, their firing off
ballistic missiles.

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:37.330
Now, here, largely in a reaction to us

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:41.467
and our Republic of Korea exercises
that we're conducting right now.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:43.669
In fact,
I think those exercises are wrapping up.

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:45.638
All right, John Kirby,
thanks for your time this morning.

00:06:45.638 --> 00:06:49.675
Joining us now from Taiwan, CNN senior
international correspondent Will Ripley.

00:06:49.976 --> 00:06:51.277
Well, hello.

00:06:51.277 --> 00:06:53.946
What should we expect to see today
in this meeting between Xi

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:55.081
and Putin?

00:06:57.683 --> 00:07:00.686
Well, certainly on the surface, it's
going to be quite a lavish affair.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:03.356
This is an official state visit
going on for three days.

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:07.727
And I bet Vladimir
Putin is very happy to see Xi Jinping.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:11.164
I mean, this is his best friend
in the world right now, considering,

00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:15.368
you know, the potential to be tried on
war crimes charges.

00:07:16.002 --> 00:07:19.372
You know, condemnation by the West,
you know, growing

00:07:19.372 --> 00:07:23.476
allegations of of just barbaric behavior
with him at the helm.

00:07:23.743 --> 00:07:27.513
And yet you have the Chinese president
showing up, talking about,

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:31.951
you know, working with Putin
to safeguard the international order,

00:07:32.151 --> 00:07:34.387
a journey of friendship,
cooperation and peace.

00:07:35.488 --> 00:07:38.090
You know, it's it's it just really is
so thick.

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:39.859
You know, you could slice it with a knife.

00:07:39.859 --> 00:07:43.629
And yet this is what, you know,
the Russian public, the Chinese public,

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:47.900
this is what they're being fed And this
and so this build up of this

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:50.403
this no limits partnership
between these two.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:55.074
Again, you know, she continues
just to really put so much you know,

00:07:55.141 --> 00:07:59.212
of head of his own credibility, really,
in this relationship with Vladimir Putin.

00:07:59.479 --> 00:08:03.082
Now, the question that we need to to see
if it will be answered publicly

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:07.153
or if it'll come out later
is whether they talk about lethal weapons,

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:10.623
which Putin needs because his troops
are running out of ammunition

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:11.591
and other things.

00:08:11.591 --> 00:08:16.128
And will China be willing to give Russia
the weapons that it would need

00:08:16.863 --> 00:08:20.032
that could actually turn turn things
around for them on the ground potentially?

00:08:20.066 --> 00:08:21.300
This is the big concern.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:24.871
And also this Chinese peace plan
that that she is going there touting.

00:08:25.238 --> 00:08:25.771
All right.

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:30.209
Basically, Ukraine says this plan
needs to begin with a Russian withdrawal.

00:08:30.243 --> 00:08:31.544
But what China is calling for

00:08:31.544 --> 00:08:35.014
is for Russia to basically be given
the land that they've already taken.

00:08:35.781 --> 00:08:36.182
Yeah.

00:08:36.182 --> 00:08:39.519
And notable, given that John Kirby
said earlier, even if China does

00:08:39.519 --> 00:08:42.755
publicly propose a cease fire, once again,
he the U.S.

00:08:42.889 --> 00:08:44.290
is Ukraine should reject it.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.492
And he said the US will reject it as well.

00:08:49.829 --> 00:08:50.930
Yeah, it's it's

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:53.733
these are two men,
two strong men up against the West.

00:08:53.733 --> 00:08:59.138
And with each visit, with each, you know,
each side is digging in their heels.

00:08:59.138 --> 00:09:02.742
It's really pretty troubling
for a lot of people watching the direction

00:09:02.742 --> 00:09:05.578
of of these two polar opposites
in the world right now.

00:09:05.745 --> 00:09:06.112
All right.

00:09:06.112 --> 00:09:08.447
Will Ripley in Taiwan for us this morning.

00:09:08.481 --> 00:09:10.449
Well, thank you
very much. Appreciate you joining us.

